{
 "thread": "_aQve9Ly4sU",
 "subject": "Log likelihood for hierarchical logistic model using ADVI",
 "messages_listed": 3,
 "last_activity": "2017-02-15T12:34:19Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "e6GpTCMAEQAJ",
   "from": "Jack Blumenau",
   "author": "42a95fb3a0b6cfb3",
   "date": "2017-02-14T15:08:23Z",
   "subject": "Log likelihood for hierarchical logistic model using ADVI",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Hi all,</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">First time posting here so apologies if I miss vital information/make stupid errors in what follows.</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">I am using ADVI (via rstan) to estimate a large heirarchical logistic regression model. The data I have is members-of-parliament-by-debate in the UK House of Commons. I have about 4m observations of whether a particular MP appeared in a particular debate, which I model as a function of MP- and debate-specific intercepts, and random effects for some predictors (the number of predictors varies according to which model I specify and is given bay the row_vector matrix X in the code below, the parameters for which are stored as Beta).</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">The model seems to estimate fine in that it gives me reasonable looking output from a substantive perspective, and does so pretty fast: about 30 minutes for a reasonably complex model. </p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">However, in order to do some model selection, I wanted to make use of the `loo` package in R. I followed the advice here (<a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/loo/vignettes/loo-example.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/loo/vignettes/loo-example.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792458569666000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2DIXJPbDjPyHqIOA9TtmSv\">https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/loo/vignettes/loo-example.html</a>) by incorporating the log likelihood into the generated quantities block. Once this is incorporated, however, the run time slows down a lot: I&#39;m now on hour six of waiting for the &quot;sampling from the approximate posterior&quot; stage to finish.</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">So, my question: am I doing something dumb here to make things slow down so much?</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Any help would be most appreciated! ADVI and Stan are great, by the way!</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Thanks,</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Jack</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">stancode &lt;- &quot;</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">data {</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">int&lt;lower = 1&gt; N_obs; // Number of observations</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">int&lt;lower = 1&gt; N; // Number of mps</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">int&lt;lower = 1&gt; D; // Number of debates</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">int&lt;lower = 1&gt; K; // Number of topics</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">int nId[N_obs];  // Unique mp id</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">int dId[N_obs]; // Unique debate id</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">int Y[N_obs]; // Response</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">row_vector[K] X[N_obs]; // Topic proportions</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">real X_sig[N_obs]; // Signatures</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">}</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">parameters {</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">real alpha[N]; // MP effect</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">real delta[D]; // Debate effect</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">real gamma; // Signature coefficient</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">vector[K] Beta[N]; // MP-topic coefficients</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">}</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">model {</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">real mu[N_obs];</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">for(i in 1:N_obs)  {</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">mu[i] = (alpha[nId[i]] + </p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">         delta[dId[i]] + </p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">         dot_product(Beta[nId[i],], X[i,]) +</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">         gamma * X_sig[i]);</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">}</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Y ~ bernoulli_logit(mu);</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">// Priors for mp intercepts</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">// Loop over MPs</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">alpha ~ normal(0, 3);</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">// Priors for debate intercepts</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">delta ~ normal(0, 3);</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">// Priors for topic-mp coefficients</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">for(k in 1:K) Beta[,k] ~ normal(0, 3);</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">// Prior for signature coefficients</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">gamma ~ normal(0, 3);</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">}</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">generated quantities {</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">   vector[N_obs] log_lik;</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> for (n in 1:N_obs) {</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> log_lik[n] = bernoulli_logit_lpmf(Y[n] | alpha[nId[n]] + delta[dId[n]] + dot_product(Beta[nId[n],], X[n,]) + gamma * X_sig[n]);</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> }</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> }</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">&quot;</p></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "xffyblcKEQAJ",
   "from": "Aki Vehtari",
   "author": "a236d3d356ca53fd",
   "date": "2017-02-14T18:15:21Z",
   "subject": "Re: Log likelihood for hierarchical logistic model using ADVI",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\">mu in model block has 4m elements, but they are not stored.</span></div><div><br></div><div>log_lik in generated quantities has 4m x (number of samples drawn from the approximate posterior) elements. I guess filling this matrix and writing it to the file takes in the current Stan version quite a long time.</div><div><br></div><div>If 10*(N+K+N*K)&lt;&lt;N_obs then you don&#39;t probably need loo</div><div><br></div><div>You could use k-fold-CV with grouping by MPs or topics, and then you could use compute mean or sum log_lik for the group, which would then need less memory.</div><div><br></div><div>Aki</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>On Tuesday, February 14, 2017 at 5:08:23 PM UTC+2, Jack Blumenau wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Hi all,</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">First time posting here so apologies if I miss vital information/make stupid errors in what follows.</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">I am using ADVI (via rstan) to estimate a large heirarchical logistic regression model. The data I have is members-of-parliament-by-debate in the UK House of Commons. I have about 4m observations of whether a particular MP appeared in a particular debate, which I model as a function of MP- and debate-specific intercepts, and random effects for some predictors (the number of predictors varies according to which model I specify and is given bay the row_vector matrix X in the code below, the parameters for which are stored as Beta).</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">The model seems to estimate fine in that it gives me reasonable looking output from a substantive perspective, and does so pretty fast: about 30 minutes for a reasonably complex model. </p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">However, in order to do some model selection, I wanted to make use of the `loo` package in R. I followed the advice here (<a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/loo/vignettes/loo-example.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/loo/vignettes/loo-example.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792458569671000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2dHQRjscF_cbkHwOupftJ2\">https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/loo/vignettes/loo-example.html</a>) by incorporating the log likelihood into the generated quantities block. Once this is incorporated, however, the run time slows down a lot: I&#39;m now on hour six of waiting for the &quot;sampling from the approximate posterior&quot; stage to finish.</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">So, my question: am I doing something dumb here to make things slow down so much?</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Any help would be most appreciated! ADVI and Stan are great, by the way!</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Thanks,</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Jack</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">stancode &lt;- &quot;</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">data {</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">int&lt;lower = 1&gt; N_obs; // Number of observations</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">int&lt;lower = 1&gt; N; // Number of mps</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">int&lt;lower = 1&gt; D; // Number of debates</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">int&lt;lower = 1&gt; K; // Number of topics</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">int nId[N_obs];  // Unique mp id</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">int dId[N_obs]; // Unique debate id</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">int Y[N_obs]; // Response</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">row_vector[K] X[N_obs]; // Topic proportions</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">real X_sig[N_obs]; // Signatures</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">}</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">parameters {</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">real alpha[N]; // MP effect</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">real delta[D]; // Debate effect</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">real gamma; // Signature coefficient</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">vector[K] Beta[N]; // MP-topic coefficients</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">}</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">model {</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">real mu[N_obs];</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">for(i in 1:N_obs)  {</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">mu[i] = (alpha[nId[i]] + </p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">         delta[dId[i]] + </p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">         dot_product(Beta[nId[i],], X[i,]) +</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">         gamma * X_sig[i]);</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">}</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Y ~ bernoulli_logit(mu);</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">// Priors for mp intercepts</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">// Loop over MPs</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">alpha ~ normal(0, 3);</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">// Priors for debate intercepts</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">delta ~ normal(0, 3);</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">// Priors for topic-mp coefficients</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">for(k in 1:K) Beta[,k] ~ normal(0, 3);</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">// Prior for signature coefficients</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">gamma ~ normal(0, 3);</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">}</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">generated quantities {</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">   vector[N_obs] log_lik;</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> for (n in 1:N_obs) {</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> log_lik[n] = bernoulli_logit_lpmf(Y[n] | alpha[nId[n]] + delta[dId[n]] + dot_product(Beta[nId[n],], X[n,]) + gamma * X_sig[n]);</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> }</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> }</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">&quot;</p></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "L0wuRWVoEQAJ",
   "from": "Jack Blumenau",
   "author": "42a95fb3a0b6cfb3",
   "date": "2017-02-15T12:34:19Z",
   "subject": "Re: Log likelihood for hierarchical logistic model using ADVI",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Thanks, Aki, that&#39;s very helpful. I&#39;ll implement the k-fold-CV you suggest.<div><br></div><div>Thanks again,</div><div><br></div><div>Jack</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>On Tuesday, February 14, 2017 at 6:15:21 PM UTC, Aki Vehtari wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\">mu in model block has 4m elements, but they are not stored.</span></div><div><br></div><div>log_lik in generated quantities has 4m x (number of samples drawn from the approximate posterior) elements. I guess filling this matrix and writing it to the file takes in the current Stan version quite a long time.</div><div><br></div><div>If 10*(N+K+N*K)&lt;&lt;N_obs then you don&#39;t probably need loo</div><div><br></div><div>You could use k-fold-CV with grouping by MPs or topics, and then you could use compute mean or sum log_lik for the group, which would then need less memory.</div><div><br></div><div>Aki<br><br>On Tuesday, February 14, 2017 at 5:08:23 PM UTC+2, Jack Blumenau wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Hi all,</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">First time posting here so apologies if I miss vital information/make stupid errors in what follows.</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">I am using ADVI (via rstan) to estimate a large heirarchical logistic regression model. The data I have is members-of-parliament-by-debate in the UK House of Commons. I have about 4m observations of whether a particular MP appeared in a particular debate, which I model as a function of MP- and debate-specific intercepts, and random effects for some predictors (the number of predictors varies according to which model I specify and is given bay the row_vector matrix X in the code below, the parameters for which are stored as Beta).</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">The model seems to estimate fine in that it gives me reasonable looking output from a substantive perspective, and does so pretty fast: about 30 minutes for a reasonably complex model. </p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">However, in order to do some model selection, I wanted to make use of the `loo` package in R. I followed the advice here (<a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/loo/vignettes/loo-example.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/loo/vignettes/loo-example.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792458569677000&amp;usg=AOvVaw277tLBCENhEyehJyrD7x4g\">https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/loo/vignettes/loo-example.html</a>) by incorporating the log likelihood into the generated quantities block. Once this is incorporated, however, the run time slows down a lot: I&#39;m now on hour six of waiting for the &quot;sampling from the approximate posterior&quot; stage to finish.</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">So, my question: am I doing something dumb here to make things slow down so much?</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Any help would be most appreciated! ADVI and Stan are great, by the way!</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Thanks,</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Jack</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">stancode &lt;- &quot;</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">data {</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">int&lt;lower = 1&gt; N_obs; // Number of observations</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">int&lt;lower = 1&gt; N; // Number of mps</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">int&lt;lower = 1&gt; D; // Number of debates</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">int&lt;lower = 1&gt; K; // Number of topics</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">int nId[N_obs];  // Unique mp id</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">int dId[N_obs]; // Unique debate id</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">int Y[N_obs]; // Response</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">row_vector[K] X[N_obs]; // Topic proportions</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">real X_sig[N_obs]; // Signatures</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">}</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">parameters {</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">real alpha[N]; // MP effect</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">real delta[D]; // Debate effect</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">real gamma; // Signature coefficient</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">vector[K] Beta[N]; // MP-topic coefficients</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">}</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">model {</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">real mu[N_obs];</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">for(i in 1:N_obs)  {</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">mu[i] = (alpha[nId[i]] + </p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">         delta[dId[i]] + </p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">         dot_product(Beta[nId[i],], X[i,]) +</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">         gamma * X_sig[i]);</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">}</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Y ~ bernoulli_logit(mu);</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">// Priors for mp intercepts</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">// Loop over MPs</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">alpha ~ normal(0, 3);</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">// Priors for debate intercepts</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">delta ~ normal(0, 3);</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">// Priors for topic-mp coefficients</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">for(k in 1:K) Beta[,k] ~ normal(0, 3);</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">// Prior for signature coefficients</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">gamma ~ normal(0, 3);</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">}</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">generated quantities {</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">   vector[N_obs] log_lik;</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> for (n in 1:N_obs) {</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> log_lik[n] = bernoulli_logit_lpmf(Y[n] | alpha[nId[n]] + delta[dId[n]] + dot_product(Beta[nId[n],], X[n,]) + gamma * X_sig[n]);</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> }</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> }</p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-left:4px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">&quot;</p></div></blockquote></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
}
